   SSeettttaabbllee CCoonntteexxtt PPaarraammeetteerrss
       These implementations  support  the  following  OOSSSSLL__PPAARRAAMM(3)  entries,
       settable for an EEVVPP__MMDD__CCTTXX with EEVVPP__MMDD__CCTTXX__sseett__ppaarraammss(3):

       "xoflen" (OOSSSSLL__DDIIGGEESSTT__PPAARRAAMM__XXOOFFLLEENN) <unsigned integer>
           Sets the digest length for extendable output functions.  The length
           of the "xoflen" parameter should not exceed that of a ssiizzee__tt.

           For  backwards  compatibility reasons the default xoflen length for
           SHAKE-128 is 16 (bytes) which results in  a  security  strength  of
           only  64 bits. To ensure the maximum security strength of 128 bits,
           the xoflen should be set to at least 32.

           For backwards compatibility reasons the default xoflen  length  for
           SHAKE-256  is  32  (bytes)  which results in a security strength of
           only 128 bits. To ensure the maximum security strength of 256 bits,
           the xoflen should be set to at least 64.

